<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate falls in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate falls in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate fell in this week's primary auction and demand rose, Banco de Mexico said.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	23.46	    -201	    23.30     23.72</p>
<p>90-Day	27.73	    -164	    27.48     27.85</p>
<p>182-Day     29.91	    -183	    29.70     30.11</p>
<p>357-Day     30.93				30.74     31.10</p>
<p>Last week the 364-day paper was assigned at 32.43 pct.</p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	900 million pesos   2.77 bln pesos     3.07</p>
<p>90-Day	900 million pesos   4.35 bln pesos     4.83</p>
<p>182-Day     900 million pesos   4.83 bln pesos     5.37</p>
<p>357-Day     600 million pesos   3.16 bln pesos     5.27</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 4.58 compared with 3.49 the week before, on demand of 11.51 billion pesos.</p>
<p>Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			  26  basis points</p>
<p>    90-Day			  12  basis points</p>
<p>    182-Day			 20  basis points</p>
<p>    357-Day			 17  basis points</p>
<p>-- Mexico City newsroom, 525 728-9559. e-mail at robert.kozak@reuters.com</p>
